 "format": "{name, note, instructable, clients?, expect: {stub, reason?}}, as in stub-vectors.json, for a reader that takes the fields feature (Pond 1.13.0). It adds one known key, fields, on a step and a sub-step, never on verify (not even null). fields is known when it is null, or when it is a list of 1 to 20 objects, each holding a string label, a string value and, optionally, a boolean copy, and nothing else. Any other fields is an unknown key at the fields itself (unknownKey:steps[0].fields, never a path inside it), so the ask is an update stub. Lengths, line breaks and duplicate labels are the Pond's check, not the reader's. Every other key follows stub-vectors.json. A reader without the fields feature skips this file and treats every fields as unknown. The Swift core has no unknown-key check yet, so every case carries clients [\"android\"].",
